nd improves immune function in (New Zealand black &#x000d7; New Zealand white)F<sub>1</sub> hybrid mice</article-title><source><italic>Arthritis &#x00026; Rheumatism</italic></source><year>1987</year><volume>30</volume><issue>5</issue><fpage>557</fpage><lpage>561</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3593437</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yoshimasu</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Kanazawa</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Mikita</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Furukawa</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The expression of histamine receptors in skin lesions of MRL/Mp-lpr/lpr mice</article-title><source><italic>The Open Dermatology Journal</italic></source><year>2008</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>83</fpage><lpage>86</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nishide</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Yoshimasu</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Ikeda</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Seo</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Ohtani</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Furukawa</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cytokine profiles of skin lesions in murine lupus models</article-title><source><italic>Journal of Dermatological Science Supplement</italic></source><year>2005</year><volume>1</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>S37</fpage><lpage>S43</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yoshimasu</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Nishide</surname><given-names>T</given-names